        ><div class="i0MChSVujGVnxxTj9" data-instant-type="container"
          ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text i0fkcaNDF2aUtebMI"><h2>This Used To Be Me.</h2></div
          ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iOcfOIY5FIXMcdo8I"><p>For years my weight was something I was always thinking about. I&apos;d lose weight, gain some back, try another approach and repeat the cycle.</p></div
          ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text is2eQJ3AggwMxzXoD"><p>Eventually I lost over 100 pounds.</p></div
          ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text i0LVCviJ8Jt8g9o9K"><p>But the biggest breakthrough wasn&apos;t just losing it.</p></div
          ><div data-instant-type="text" class="instant-rich-text iSgIZMe4aXsEHu6CW"><p>It was finally reaching a point where staying slim stopped feeling like something I had to fight for every day.</p></div></div
